jumbit 0.1.2 — a MoonBit rewrite of zoxide

Usage:
  jumbit add [--score N] <path>...        record directories (--score sets this visit's weight)
  jumbit remove <path>...                 remove directories from the database
  jumbit query [kw]...                    print the highest-scoring match
    --list                                print all matches (by score, descending)
    --score                               prefix each line with its score
    --all                                 skip the existence check
    --exclude <path>                      exclude a path (exact match)
    --interactive                         select interactively with fzf
    --json                                print all matches as a single-line JSON array (agent channel, mutually exclusive with --interactive)
    --fuzzy                               fall back to component substrings when exact matching finds nothing (jumbit extension)
    --tsv                                 print Tab-separated path/score/last_accessed/matched_by (jumbit extension, mutually exclusive with --json/--interactive)
    --limit <n>                           print only the first n entries (with --list/--json/--tsv, jumbit extension)
  jumbit init <shell>                     generate shell integration code (defines j/ji by default, hook=pwd)
    [--cmd C] [--hook pwd|prompt|none] [--no-cmd]
  jumbit import <plugin> [--merge]        import history data from other tools (empty database imports directly, --merge merges into a non-empty one)
  jumbit describe <path> [--note text]    show or set a human note (--note "" clears, jumbit extension)
  jumbit export --agents                  print the project map as Markdown (paste into AGENTS.md, jumbit extension)
    plugin ∈ atuin/autojump/fasd/z/z.lua/zsh-z (bad lines are reported one by one, never aborting)
  jumbit status [--json] [--check]        database self-check: entries/notes/format/threshold (--check scans existence, --json for agents, jumbit extension)
  jumbit mcp                              start the stdio MCP server (agent channel, tools: jumbit_query / jumbit_export_agents, jumbit extension)
  jumbit edit                             edit the database with $VISUAL/$EDITOR (jumbit extension)
    [--rename <old> <new>] | [--prune]    rename a path (notes follow) / drop nonexistent entries; mutually exclusive
  jumbit help                             print this help
  jumbit --version                        print version (-V works too)

Environment variables:
  _JB_DATA_DIR                            data directory (default $HOME/.local/share/jumbit, must be absolute)
  _JB_ECHO=1                              echo directories as they are recorded
  _JB_EXCLUDE_DIRS                        colon-separated glob list, matched paths are kept out of the database
  _JB_FZF_OPTS                            extra arguments passed through to fzf
  _JB_RESOLVE_SYMLINKS=1                  resolve symlinks when recording (queries do not follow them)
  _JB_MAXAGE=N                            aging threshold for the database total score (default 10000)
import reads each plugin's standard data file, located via _Z_DATA/_FASD_DATA/ZSHZ_DATA/_ZL_DATA/XDG_DATA_HOME
